WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.444
Begin with the selected area and UTC window. Show the recorded satellite observations

2
00:00:08.444 --> 00:00:15.000
and make clear that the map is a study view, not a fire perimeter.

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:25.820
Show the dated activity with its unit and fixed scale. Identify any estimated or unknown

4
00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:30.000
dates before drawing a comparison.

5
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.514
Show why a blank record can remain unknown. Collected exports, documented processing

6
00:00:38.514 --> 00:00:45.000
gaps and actual observation opportunity are different questions.

7
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:55.645
Present the checked finding, then open its evidence. Keep the explanatory interpretation

8
00:00:55.645 --> 00:01:00.000
distinct from the saved measurement.

9
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Show an original reading and its acquisition time. Explain why a source row and an

10
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.000
occupied common cell are different units.

11
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:23.156
Close with the supported observation and the matching evidence download. Keep ignition,

12
00:01:23.156 --> 00:01:30.000
continuous spread, perimeter and forecast claims outside the conclusions.
